<% content_for :page_title, 'Live rooms · Media Studio' %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag '/lightek/media-control.css?v=61' %>
<% installing=@installing %>
<main class="media-control media-setup" <%= 'data-media-installing=true' if installing %>>
  <header class="mc-top"><%= link_to 'LIGHTEK / MEDIA STUDIO', dashboard_media_studio_path(site_id:@site.id),class:'mc-brand' %><%= link_to 'Back to Studio',dashboard_media_studio_path(site_id:@site.id),class:'mc-button' %></header>
  <section class="mc-setup-intro"><span class="mc-eyebrow">LIVE PRODUCTION</span><h1>Bring everyone into the room.</h1><p>Set up voice, video and screen sharing for <strong><%= @site.name %></strong>. Bring the room into your Studio program when you’re ready to go live.</p></section>
  <div class="mc-setup-grid"><section class="mc-panel"><div class="mc-panel-heading"><h2>Live rooms setup</h2><span class="mc-status"><%= @state['status']=='ready' ? 'Ready' : installing ? 'Setting up' : @state['status']=='failed' ? 'Needs attention' : 'Not connected' %></span></div>
    <ol class="mc-steps"><li><b>Connect this website</b><span><%= @site.host %> · <%= @installation ? @installation.gatekeeper_node.name : 'Choose its existing server below' %></span></li><li><b>Set up the room service</b><span>We create its private credentials and configure the media service.</span></li><li><b>Verify the connection</b><span>We check HTTPS and report whether your rooms are ready.</span></li></ol>
    <% if @state['status']=='failed' %><p class="mc-alert" role="alert"><%= @state['message'].presence || 'The previous setup did not complete. Retry using the connected server below.' %></p><% end %>
    <% if installing %><div class="mc-progress" role="status"><span></span><div><strong>Setting up live rooms…</strong><p>This can take a few minutes. You can keep working in Studio.</p></div></div><%= link_to 'Check status',dashboard_session_media_path(site_id:@site.id),class:'mc-button' %>
    <% elsif @installation %><p class="mc-server"><strong><%= @installation.gatekeeper_node.name %></strong><span>Existing website server · <%= @site.host %></span></p><%= button_to(@state['status']=='ready' ? 'Verify live rooms' : 'Set up live rooms',install_dashboard_session_media_path(site_id:@site.id,installation_id:@installation.id),class:'mc-button mc-primary',data:{turbo:false}) %>
    <% elsif @projects.any? %><%= form_with url:install_dashboard_session_media_path(site_id:@site.id),method: :post,local:true,data:{turbo:false} do %><label class="mc-field"><span>Website server</span><%= select_tag :project_id,options_for_select(@projects.map{|p|["#{p.gatekeeper_node.name} · #{p.domain}",p.id]}) %></label><p class="mc-muted">Connects the existing application and starts setup. No new server is purchased.</p><%= submit_tag 'Connect & set up live rooms',class:'mc-button mc-primary' %><% end %>
    <% else %><p class="mc-alert">This website has no connected application runtime yet.</p><%= link_to 'Connect an existing server',dashboard_servers_path(site_id:@site.id),class:'mc-button mc-primary' %><p class="mc-muted">Open your server, connect this website’s application, then return here. The website hostname must be <strong><%= @site.host %></strong>.</p><% end %>
  </section><aside class="mc-panel mc-setup-aside"><span class="mc-eyebrow">ONE PRODUCTION</span><h2>From conversation to broadcast.</h2><p>Invite guests through reservations, admit them to a room, and bring their individual cameras and audio into Live Studio.</p><ul><li>Voice and multiperson video</li><li>Screen sharing and host controls</li><li>Branded stages and guest layouts</li><li>Studio output to your live destinations</li></ul><details><summary>Server & network details</summary><p>Requires a connected Ubuntu/Apache application with HTTPS and at least 2 GB RAM. Setup configures the host firewall for TCP 7881, UDP 3478 and UDP 50000–50100. An external provider firewall must also allow these ports. Restrictive networks requiring TURN/TLS need a separate relay configuration.</p></details></aside></div>
</main>
<% if installing %><script>setTimeout(()=>location.reload(),10000);</script><% end %>
